.TH SITUC 1 "" "situ" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
situc \- compiler for situ byte-layout schemas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B situc
.RI [ --diagnostics
.IR text | json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I schema
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B situ
is a schema language for data whose layout is decided by somebody else:
network protocols, file formats and device registers, where the bytes are
fixed and the reader has to match them exactly. A schema states what the
bytes are, and
.B situc
derives everything else from it.
.PP
What it derives is not only accessors. A schema also produces a capability
map saying what each field costs to reach, a byte-level wire contract that
makes an incompatible edit visible in review, a Wireshark dissector, a fuzz
harness, and a test suite holding the generated code to the map.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Generate accessors.
.B \-\-owned
additionally emits, for each fixed-size layout, a plain C struct and a
decode that copies every field into it -- for callers that hold the value
after the buffer is gone.
.B \-\-single\-file
inlines the parts of the Python runtime the schema reaches, so the output
is one module importing only the standard library.
.B \-\-target
selects
.IR c ", " cpp ", " rust " or " python ;
.B \-\-out
names the output directory.
.B \-\-layer
chooses how much of the schema becomes code, each rung emitting everything
below it:
.I view
is accessors over bytes the caller owns and is the default, and
.I relate
adds one predicate per declared relation, over two views the caller already
holds. The remaining rungs --
.IR edit ", " frame ", " converse " and " drive
-- are decided and not built, and asking for one says which phase adds it.
.TP
.B map
Emit the capability map, or with
.B \-\-check
compare against the committed one.
.TP
.B wire
Emit the byte-level contract, or with
.B \-\-check
classify what an edit changed.
.TP
.B verify
Check that a corpus of real bytes conforms to the schema, generating
nothing. For using a schema as a specification rather than as the source of
the code: see
.B situ
project.md 26.67.
.TP
.B pack
Emit the packed layout image: the placements with their kinds, offsets,
sizes and endianness, plus a bytecode for the expression language of
section 10. A walker in another project reads one to parse a format it was
not compiled against; nothing in
.B situc
walks an image. The format is described by
.I std/image.situ
and read through generated accessors.
.B \-o
writes to a file rather than to standard output, which is binary.
.B \-\-metadata
appends names and capability vectors, which a tooling walker wants and a
device does not.
.B \-\-coverage
reports what went into the image, and exits non-zero if anything could not
be encoded, rather than emitting it. See project.md 26.33 and
docs/decisions/0026-runtime-image-and-interpreter.md.
.TP
.B doc
RFC-style byte-layout diagrams and a field reference.
.TP
.B explain
One path's capability vector and the blame chain behind it.
.TP
.B advise
Ranked, costed suggestions for a schema.
.TP
.B diff
Capability changes between two revisions of a schema.
.TP
.B gen-checks
Tests holding the generated accessors to the capability map.
.TP
.B gen-fuzz
A fuzz harness per parseable struct.
.TP
.B gen-dissector
A Wireshark dissector in Lua.
.TP
.B gen-tests
Golden-vector tests from a
.I .vectors
file.
.TP
.B gen-codec-tests
Property tests from codec signatures.
.TP
.B gen-derived
Implementations from kernel descriptions.
.TP
.B import-proto
Import a
.I .proto
as a description of its wire format.
.TP
.B dump-ast
Print the parsed AST, as a tree or back as situ source.
.TP
.B lsp
Run a language server over stdio.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR
Diagnostic output format.
.I json
is for editors and CI.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B situc
exits 0 when it accepted the schema and did what was asked, and non-zero
when it refused. A refusal is a diagnostic with a blame chain, not a stack
trace.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/situc/std
Standard schemas, including the codec signatures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The generated C requires the header and static library in
.BR libsitu-dev .
